  "outline": [
    "Question clip (hand-made 25 Oct 2026, the word-problem shape of log-scales-am): the question read; the plan pinned in the corner: x → dx/dt → d²x/dt² (differentiate once for velocity, again for acceleration).",
    "First, what the question says: x = a sin nt, each letter lit and its meaning written; the picture A — O — B, 120 cm across, O the centre, 60 each side.",
    "(a) sin is between −1 and 1, so x is between −a and a: a is the furthest the dot goes from O = 120/2 = 60. Period of sin nt is 2π/n (why: a written drop-down) = 6, so n = π/3 (a simple solve, one step); x = 60 sin(πt/3).",
    "(b) v = dx/dt = 60 cos(πt/3) × π/3 = 20π cos(πt/3); cos is between −1 and 1, so the maximum speed = 20π × 1 = 20π cm/s.",
    "(c) d²x/dt² = dv/dt = −20π sin(πt/3) × π/3 = −(20π²/3) sin(πt/3). THE TRAP (where the student stopped): we do not need t. At A the dot is at the END of the swing: the picture again with x = −60 at A (B the positive side); 60 sin(πt/3) = −60, so sin(πt/3) = −1; acceleration = −(20π²/3)(−1) = 20π²/3 = 65.8 cm/s² (3 s.f.). Why not t = 1.5: a written drop-down (that time is the other end, B — same size)."
  ],
